A||N||6||johnmac||DUMB Alternator Question||||10||
Z||000000||johnmac||09-08-2001||11:29 PM||||Please excuse this dumb question about the alternator as electricity is not my strong suit.<P>Is the Alternator Battery Post and Post 2 (+) connected of the connected to ground?<P>When I check my old and new alternator, they both show a connection to the casing. <P>Consequently my Battery terminal connections (+) & (-)indicate a connection. <P>Using the buzzer on the meter it works only in one direction. If I change my red & black feelers - No buzzer.<P>What is going on?<P><P>------------------<BR>John MacHaffie<BR>86GT "Yellowbird"<BR>12+ month project car<BR>johnmac@mpinet.net<BR>Winter Springs, Florida||||reg||10
Z||000001||Fierowrecker||09-09-2001||04:10 PM||||Hey John!<BR>The Batt terminal is positive, the 1 and 2 terminals go off to the wiring harness (Idiot light and ignition switch)<BR>What you are seeing with the meter, is diode action... Totally normal...<BR>The alt. case is ground or negitive...<BR>crash...||||reg||1
Z||000002||samoht||09-09-2001||04:16 PM||||that positive to the alternator is hot all the time, so dont forget to unhook your negitive to the battery...   That booted wire can NOT touch the caseing of the alt.  good luck..  Ebay some nice powder coated 105 alt. for 70 bucks I think||||reg||1
Z||000003||johnmac||09-10-2001||12:08 AM||||DIODE ACTION <P>That must be it. Thanks for the quick comeback.<P>John<P>------------------<BR>John MacHaffie<BR>86GT "Yellowbird"<BR>12+ month project car<BR>johnmac@mpinet.net<BR>Winter Springs, Florida||||reg||1
Z||000004||SLYGUY||09-10-2001||01:09 AM||||Just replaced my alternator. <BR>105 amp. for $109. <P>Not a difficult job if you remove the jack it up and use jackstands too!!, remove the right rear tire. About 2-3 hours work and worked like a charm. <BR>Oh, did I mention that this solved the whirring dry bearing sound that developed a few days before the battery died? It did and I was afraid that that sound meant something major. Whew!!<P>Sly||||reg||14
Z||000005||SLYGUY||09-10-2001||01:10 AM||||I meant not a difficult job if you remove the TIRE, not the jack. Use both a good jack on the frame, and jackstands.<P>Sly||||reg||1
Z||000006||johnmac||09-10-2001||09:11 AM||||I removed my alternator both ways.<P>Taking it from the top is easier if you have an automatic transmisson.<P>Remove the dogbone, alternator bracket, cooling tube and water hose.<P>It will slide out if you remove the heat shield.<P><P>------------------<BR>John MacHaffie<BR>86GT "Yellowbird"<BR>12+ month project car<BR>johnmac@mpinet.net<BR>Winter Springs, Florida||||reg||1
